@startuml dict-build
' DictionaryBuilder: two entry points, one shared four-step construction, and the
' invariant that makes rank() free — entries are sorted by descending frequency.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/dict-build.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/dictionary/building.md, section "The build, step by step".
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
}
title DictionaryBuilder — from counts to a frequency-ranked, read-only dictionary

rectangle "**build_from_extractor(&WordExtractor)**\nN = extractor.total_tokens()\n(every token the extractor accepted)" as bfe #546E7A
rectangle "**build_from_counts(HashMap<String, u64>)**\nN = Σ counts.values()\n(including words about to be filtered out)" as bfc #546E7A

rectangle "**1 · threshold**\nkeep w iff f(w) ≥ min_frequency\n(default 1 — i.e. keep everything)" as st1 #1565C0
rectangle "**2 · score**\nlog_prob(w) = ln(f(w) / N)  if compute_log_probs\nelse None" as st2 #1565C0
rectangle "**3 · sort**\nentries.sort_by(|a, b| b.frequency.cmp(&a.frequency))\nO(V log V) — descending" as st3 #1565C0
rectangle "**4 · index**\nword_index : HashMap<String, usize>\ni ↦ position in the sorted Vec" as st4 #1565C0

rectangle "**DictionaryMetadata**\nversion = 1 · language · word_count\ntotal_tokens = N · min_frequency\ncreated_at = now() · source" as meta #1565C0

rectangle "**SpellingDictionary**" as sd #00838F
rectangle "**rank(w) = word_index[w]**\n0 = most frequent — the index **is** the Zipf rank" as rank #455A64

bfe --> st1
bfc --> st1
st1 --> st2
st2 --> st3
st3 --> st4
st4 --> sd
meta --> sd
sd --> rank

note right of st2
  **N is the pre-threshold token count.** Words dropped in
  step 1 still sit in the denominator, so the retained mass
  Σ p(w) over the kept words is **< 1** whenever
  min_frequency > 1. The deficit is exactly the OOV mass —
  a feature for back-off scoring, a trap if you assume the
  dictionary is a normalised distribution.
end note

note bottom of sd
  **merge(&other) re-bases the denominator.** It sums per-word
  frequencies, then sets total_tokens = Σ of the **merged, retained**
  frequencies — not N_A + N_B. Every log_prob is recomputed against
  that new N, so probabilities from a merged dictionary are not
  comparable with those of its parents.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Role |
  |<#546E7A> | entry points |
  |<#1565C0> | statistical construction |
  |<#00838F> | the built dictionary (storage) |
  |<#455A64> | what callers use it for |
endlegend
@enduml
